      "actualOutput": "Certainly! Here are some resources that can help you learn more about video editing:\n\n1. **Online Courses:**\n   - **Coursera** and **Udemy** offer a variety of courses on video editing, covering different software like Adobe Premiere Pro, Final Cut Pro, and DaVinci Resolve.\n   - **LinkedIn Learning** provides courses that range from beginner to advanced levels, often taught by industry professionals.\n\n2. **YouTube Channels:**\n   - **Peter McKinnon** and **Film Riot** are popular channels that offer tutorials and tips on video editing and filmmaking.\n   - **Premiere Gal** focuses on Adobe Premiere Pro tutorials and creative editing techniques.\n\n3. **Books:**\n   - \"The Art of Editing\" by Walter Murch is a great read for understanding the theory and practice of film editing.\n   - \"In the Blink of an Eye\" also by Walter Murch, offers insights into the philosophy and techniques of editing.\n\n4. **Online Communities:**\n   - **Reddit** has several subreddits like r/editors and r/VideoEditing where you can ask questions and share knowledge with other editors.\n   - **Creative COW** is a forum where professionals discuss various aspects of video production and editing.\n\n5",
